Explanation:
Key Concept: NumPy broadcasting.
Case (4,3) + (3,): Works because (3,) broadcasts across the last dimension → each row adds [1,1,1].
Case (4,3) + (4,1): Works because (4,1) broadcasts across columns → each row gets its own scalar added.
Case (2,3,4) + (3,1): Works because dimensions align after broadcasting: (2,3,4) vs (3,1) → the (3,1) expands to (2,3,4).
Case (4,3) + (4,): Fails because (4,) cannot align with (4,3) — the last dimensions 3 and 4 are incompatible
